# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-08-08 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection is surgical rather than a wholesale revert, because the three
# defects it reintroduces are three INDEPENDENT properties of the same file and
# a wholesale revert would not tell them apart:
#
#   1. `AnchoredManagedRoot::open` goes back to ONE `open(O_NOFOLLOW)` of the
#      whole path, so `<home>/worktrees` is resolved by pathname and followed.
#   2. The identity comparisons come out of `remove_dir_all_at`,
#      `reclaim_managed_worktree` and `assert_path_names`, so the entry NAME is
#      the reference point again and a substituted directory is deleted.
#   3. The reclaim loop prints `KEPT` unconditionally, so a removal that already
#      destroyed files reports the tree as intact.
#
# Nothing in the daemon is touched. Finding 6's fix lives there and is covered
# by the supervisor's own tests; see `cmd` for why it is not replayed here.
exit: 101

# ===== FINDING 4: an ANCESTOR symlink is followed ==========================
#
# The first failing assertion of its test: a sentinel laid down OUTSIDE the
# managed root, behind the symlinked `<home>/worktrees`, is gone. The mechanism
# is in the same panic — two `RECLAIMED` lines print paths under
# `<home>/worktrees/orgasmic/` while the directories those paths resolved to
# belonged to the victim. `<home>/worktrees/orgasmic` is NOT itself a symlink in
# this fixture, which is what the round-1 regression could not catch.
contains: an ancestor symlink must never redirect the scan or the removal outside the root
contains: victim/orgasmic/task-precious/keep-me.txt is gone
contains: PRUNE_SUMMARY RECLAIMED=2

# ===== FINDING 5: the identity classified is not the identity deleted ======
#
# The prune parks at its post-reservation rendezvous; the classified worktree is
# moved aside and a different directory takes its name. Without the identity
# carried from enumeration to removal, the resumed prune deletes whatever now
# answers to that name and reports it RECLAIMED.
contains: the substituted directory must survive
contains: RECLAIMED PATH=
contains: PRUNE_SUMMARY RECLAIMED=1

# ===== "KEPT" DID NOT MEAN UNTOUCHED =======================================
#
# The removal unlinks the entries sorted before an unwritable subdirectory,
# fails on that subdirectory's contents, and reports the worktree KEPT — while
# the files it already deleted are gone.
contains: a removal that destroyed something must be reported as PARTIAL
contains: KEPT PATH=

# All three, and only these three. A binary that collapses wholesale is a
# different failure and has not reproduced what this artifact claims.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 3 failed
